31--> Public IP vs Private IP
	  -->
		Private IP address
		Used to communicate within a local network, such as your home Wi-Fi.
		Example: 192.168.1.10
		Usually not directly reachable from the public internet.

		Public IP address
		Used for internet communication and assigned or routed by an internet provider or cloud network.
		Example: 8.8.8.8
		Can be reachable from the internet if routing and firewall rules allow it.

		For example, your laptop might have a private IP such as 192.168.1.10, while your router uses a public IP for internet communication. 
		
		
